    fb0: "I value the reassurance of following through. When plans change, letting each other know feels better than leaving someone guessing.",
    fb1: "When trouble comes, finding a way through together and owning our parts makes me feel we are on the same side.",
    fb2: "Bad moods happen. I would rather return to the issue after we have settled than let an argument become an injury to each other.",
    fb3: "Care need not be counted gesture by gesture, but I hope sharing, support and thoughtfulness can flow both ways.",
    fb4: "Honesty and ethical limits matter to me. Reaching a result through genuine effort makes it easier to trust the relationship.",
    fb5: "When we disagree, I welcome a direct truth and want to express my own thoughts carefully, with less guessing between us.",
    fc0: "People who remain curious about the world draw me in. We can exchange things we have read or learned, beyond familiar topics.",
    fc1: "Growth need not happen at the same speed. I like moving forward separately and sometimes pausing to share changes, uncertainties and discoveries.",
    fc2: "Different views can make a conversation richer. I want to hear another explanation, not turn every discussion into a contest.",
    fc3: "A response about a small plan, or a word during a busy stretch: details like these gradually build trust.",
    fc4: "Closeness does not erase boundaries. I hope both of us can say no, spend time alone and keep a life of our own.",
